Silinex Global PHP Clone - Detailed Project Explanation

Project Overview
This project is a PHP-based clone website inspired by the Silinex Global Services website. The goal of the project is to recreate the same kind of company website structure while giving it a fresh visual theme, new colors, and a clean modern layout.

The website is built as a single-page PHP website. It includes all major sections that a professional IT consulting and staffing company website usually needs, such as a hero section, services, company introduction, industries, technologies, testimonials, FAQ, blogs, contact section, and footer.


Main Files in the Project

1. index.php
This is the main file of the website. It contains both the PHP data and the HTML structure.

At the top of the file, PHP arrays are used to store repeated content such as:
- Services
- Industries
- Technologies
- Testimonials
- FAQ questions and answers
- Blog posts

Using arrays makes the website easier to update. For example, if you want to add a new service, you only need to add one more item inside the services array instead of manually copying and pasting a full HTML card.

The rest of the file contains the HTML layout. PHP foreach loops are used to display repeated sections dynamically.


2. style.css
This file controls the full design of the website.

It includes:
- Theme colors
- Header styling
- Hero section layout
- Service cards
- Industry cards
- Technology tags
- Testimonial layout
- FAQ styling
- Blog cards
- Contact section
- Footer styling
- Responsive design for tablets and mobile devices

The website uses a new color theme based on green, coral, mint, gold, white, and dark blue-green tones. This gives the clone a different look from the original website while keeping the professional business feel.


3. README.md
This file gives basic instructions for running the project locally using PHP.


