How PHP Is Used
PHP is mainly used to avoid repeating HTML manually.

For example, instead of writing every service card separately, the project stores service information inside an array:

$services = [
    [
        'title' => 'Staffing',
        'text' => 'End-to-end technology staffing...',
        'icon' => '01'
    ],
];

Then the foreach loop displays each service:

foreach ($services as $service) {
    echo the service card
}

This same method is used for industries, technologies, testimonials, FAQs, and blogs.

This makes the website:
- Easier to edit
- Easier to expand
- Cleaner to maintain
- Less repetitive


Security Note
The website uses htmlspecialchars() when printing dynamic content.

This is useful because it converts special characters into safe HTML entities. It helps prevent unwanted HTML or script code from being executed if the content changes in the future.

Example:

<?php echo htmlspecialchars($service['title']); ?>


